1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:04,000
See grease flung inside your wheel?
That's not dirt.

2
00:00:04,000 --> 00:00:09,000
A torn CV boot slings grease everywhere it can reach —
and doesn't make a sound yet.

3
00:00:09,000 --> 00:00:15,000
One clue: no clicking yet doesn't mean it's fine —
the joint fails once the grease is gone and dirt gets in.

4
00:00:15,000 --> 00:00:21,000
By the time you hear a click on turns,
the joint itself may already be damaged — the boot was the warning.

5
00:00:21,000 --> 00:00:26,000
Worth checking during a routine rotation,
before it turns into a full axle replacement.

6
00:00:26,000 --> 00:00:30,000
Stop by and we'll take a look.
Nick's Tire & Auto.
